A||N||1||DaveL||700 TBI on 2.5 DIS||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||02-16-2000||08:54 AM||||I want to rework the IAC and fuel injector on my 87 SE 2.5 but the Haynes manual has no illustrations for this. Are the procedures pretty much the same? Kits are available for about $32 locally, but I'll of course want to replace the injector, and maybe the fuel pressure regulator. Is the measurement for the IAC total length the same? And just how delicate is the IAC?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||02-16-2000||09:11 AM||||There is a haynes book covering fuel injection from 86-92(I think that's the range) that covers both the 300 and 700 TBI.<P>The IAC preinstalled length is about the same. make it even shorter won't hurt any, it just can't exceed that lenght. The IAC is fairly strudy but won't tolerate direct abuse. DO NOT soak IAC motors or TPS in solvent. If the IAC won't drop fully into the hole by hand something is wrong.<P>The rework kit will come with the fuel pressure diaphram. and all o rings, gaskets, and screens.<P>Do the rework and the IAC at the same time. Try doing just that before replacing the injector. The injector can be repaced in a couple minutes, and with the TBI installed on the car, if you still think it needs to be done. The rework kit comes with injector screens and seals, use these to replace the original ones on the old injector.  <P>Use the body and base gaskets that match the original ones. DO NOT use sealler on any gaskets. DO lube all O ring seals with a drop of ATF before installing them.<P>You MUST use 2 wrenches to separate and install the fuel lines or you could damage the TBI body. Ideally you will use a flare wrench on this hardware. remove the 13mm bolt holding the fuel lines to the manifold to make it easier working with the lines durring reassembly.<P>DO NOT over tighten the air cleaner bolt/studs or you can strip the holes in the intake manifold. Lubricate the air cleanner bolts before installing them to prevent galling.(I use antisieze on these bolts only. all other screws/holes should just be cleaned.)||||reg||1
